    ".claude/commands/load_ai_docs.md": "SUB-AGENT delegation: reads ai_docs/README.md, deletes docs older than 24h, and fires @agent-docs-scraper in parallel via the Task tool (one per URL). allowed-tools include Task and mcp__firecrawl-mcp__firecrawl_scrape.",
    ".claude/commands/load_bundle.md": "Reloads a context bundle: dedups JSONL entries per file_path, picks the most comprehensive read (full file if any entry has no limit/offset), and replays the prior agent's story without acting on logged prompts.",
    ".claude/commands/experts/cc_hook_expert/cc_hook_expert_plan.md": "AGENT EXPERT (plan): a Claude Code hook specialist that reads ai_docs hooks/uv/slash-command guides, analyzes existing hooks, and writes a spec to specs/experts/cc_hook_expert/<name>.md. Carries a dedicated ## Expertise section (hook events, execution model, output patterns, security) that already contains 'Discovered Patterns from Universal Logger Implementation' — evidence the improve step ran.",
    ".claude/commands/experts/cc_hook_expert/cc_hook_expert_build.md": "AGENT EXPERT (build): implements a hook from a spec, chmod +x, and tests via `echo '<json>' | uv run .claude/hooks/<hook>.py`. Its ## Expertise section holds UV-script standards, exit-code/JSON output patterns, and 'Learned Best Practices from Recent Implementations.'",
    ".claude/commands/experts/cc_hook_expert/cc_hook_expert_improve.md": "AGENT EXPERT (improve): the self-improving meta-step. Runs git diff / git diff --cached / git log, and updates ONLY the ## Expertise sections of the plan and build experts (explicitly NOT the Workflow sections). If no relevant learnings: stop and report 'No expertise updates needed.'",
    ".claude/agents/docs-scraper.md": "Sub-agent (model sonnet): scrapes a URL via firecrawl (fallback WebFetch) and writes clean markdown to ai_docs/. Invoked in parallel by /load_ai_docs.",
    ".claude/agents/research-docs-fetcher.md": "Sub-agent named 'research-agent' (model sonnet): fetches/searches and writes structured markdown with metadata headers to ai_docs/research/, skipping files <24h old.",
    ".claude/agents/meta-agent.md": "Sub-agent (model opus): an agent architect that generates brand-new sub-agent definition files from a description (scrapes current sub-agent docs first). Shows the 'agents that build agents' idea.",
    ".claude/hooks/context_bundle_builder.py": "UV single-file hook. On Read/Write (file_ops) logs {operation, file_path(relative), limit/offset or content_length}; on UserPromptSubmit logs {operation: prompt, prompt[:500]}. Appends to agents/context_bundles/<DAY_HOUR>_<session_id>.jsonl. Powers technique #8.",
    ".claude/hooks/universal_hook_logger.py": "UV single-file hook wired to every event; writes {timestamp, payload} to agents/hook_logs/<session_id>/<hook_event_name>.jsonl. Non-blocking (always exit 0). The observability layer the cc_hook_expert demo builds/extends.",
    ".claude/output-styles/concise-done.md": "'One Word Output' style: respond only 'Done.' 95% of the time; exceptions for explicit requests, questions (1-2 sentences), and errors. The 2-token response in the output-tokens demo.",
    ".claude/output-styles/concise-ultra.md": "'Ultra Concise' style: absolute minimum words, fragments over sentences, tool outputs without commentary.",
    ".claude/output-styles/concise-tts.md": "'TTS Summary' style: ultra-concise text, then runs .claude/utils/tts/elevenlabs_tts.py with a <15-word spoken summary addressed to USER_NAME (Dan).",
    ".claude/output-styles/verbose-bullet-points.md": "'Bullet Points' style: hierarchical bullets for quick scanning (a verbose counterpart shown in the /output-style menu).",
    ".claude/output-styles/verbose-yaml-structured.md": "'YAML Structured' style: structured YAML with hierarchical key/value pairs.",
    ".claude/utils/llm/{anth.py,oai.py,ollama.py}": "Minimal LLM helper utilities (Anthropic / OpenAI / Ollama) available to hooks and TTS scripts.",
    ".claude/utils/tts/{elevenlabs_tts.py,openai_tts.py,pyttsx3_tts.py}": "Text-to-speech utilities used by the concise-tts output style.",
    "apps/hello_cc_1.ts": "Claude Code TypeScript SDK hello-world: query() with model sonnet, prints result + cost/duration/turns/session id. Demonstrates the SDK the wrapper is built on.",
    "apps/hello_cc_2.ts": "Second SDK hello-world variant (maxTurns 1, allowedTools []) — the 'hello calls' Dan references before building the wrapper.",
    "apps/cc_ts_wrapper/index.ts": "Bare `bun init` stub (console.log('Hello via Bun!')) — the scaffold the planner/builder demo fills in.",
    "apps/cc_ts_wrapper/types.ts": "The TYPES file the demo builds: ClaudeSettings, AdhocPromptOptions, ReusablePromptConfig, PromptResult, and DEFAULT_SETTINGS (maxTurns 5, allowedTools Bash/Read/Write/Edit/WebSearch).",
    "apps/cc_ts_wrapper/core.ts": "The LOW-LEVEL wrapper the demo builds: adhoc_prompt(), register_prompt(), reusable_prompt(), list_commands() over query() from @anthropic-ai/claude-code, capturing result messages and session id.",
    "apps/cc_ts_wrapper/cli.ts": "The CLI the demo builds: parseArgs, built-in /analyze and /refactor registered prompts, --command/--prompt/--max-turns/--system-prompt/--tools/--list/--help. The 'types file, low-level file, CLI file' three-file wrapper Dan specifies.",
    "apps/cc_ts_wrapper/README.md": "Default bun-init README (bun install / bun run index.ts).",
    "apps/cc_ts_wrapper/CLAUDE.md": "Bun-focused local memory file (use bun over node, Bun.serve, bun:sqlite, etc.) — a scoped memory file for the sub-app.",
    "apps/cc_ts_wrapper/{package.json,tsconfig.json,.gitignore}": "bun-init scaffolding for the wrapper app.",
    "ai_docs/README.md": "The URL list /load_ai_docs scrapes: Claude Code SDK (headless/python/typescript), MCP, slash-commands, sub-agents, models overview, hooks, and UV scripts/projects guides.",
    "scripts/bg_claude_code_test.sh": "Raw shell version of primary delegation: a bg() function running `claude --print --model <m> --output-format text --dangerously-skip-permissions --mcp-config .mcp.json --append-system-prompt \"<report + rename logic>\" \"<prompt>\"`."
  },
  "generated_not_committed": {
    "agents/context_bundles/<DAY_HOUR>_<session_id>.jsonl": "Per-session append-only context bundles written by context_bundle_builder.py (e.g. SAT_12_<uuid>.jsonl). Reloaded with /load_bundle.",
    "agents/hook_logs/<session_id>/<hook_event_name>.jsonl": "Per-session, per-hook event logs written by universal_hook_logger.py (the observability structure the cc_hook_expert demo produces).",
    "agents/background/background-report-<DAY_HH_MM_SS>.md(.complete.md/.failed.md)": "Report files written by /background primary agents; renamed on success/failure.",
    "specs/<name>.md and specs/experts/cc_hook_expert/<name>.md": "Implementation specs written by /quick-plan and the cc_hook_expert planner.",
    "ai_docs/*.md": "Documentation scraped at runtime by docs-scraper sub-agents (deleted/refreshed after 24h)."
  }
}
