     <article class="chapter-feature">
       <div class="chapter-feature__copy">
-        <p class="eyebrow">Now available · Volume II · Lesson 11</p>
-        <h2>Building Domain-Specific Agents</h2>
-        <p class="chapter-feature__dek">Control context, model, prompt, and tools in code; climb an eight-agent ladder from Pong to a producer/consumer log system; and learn when not to build custom.</p>
-        <ul class="chapter-feature__meta"><li>Tactic · Build Custom Agents</li><li>90–150 min core lab</li><li>12 full-width course frames</li><li>2 verified practice overlays</li></ul>
-        <a class="button" href="vol-2-ah/11-building-domain-specific-agents.html">Start chapter →</a>
+        <p class="eyebrow">Now available · Volume II · Chapter 09</p>
+        <h2>Elite Context Engineering</h2>
+        <p class="chapter-feature__dek">Measure the window, master Reduce and Delegate, and progress through twelve techniques—from scoped MCP and task primes to bundles, background primaries, and self-improving agent experts.</p>
+        <ul class="chapter-feature__meta"><li>R&amp;D · Reduce + Delegate</li><li>75–120 min core lab</li><li>12 full-width course frames</li><li>4 levels · 12 techniques</li></ul>
+        <a class="button" href="vol-2-ah/09-rd-framework-context-window-mastery.html">Start chapter →</a>
       </div>
-      <div class="chapter-feature__map" aria-label="Agentic path visual">
